      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, you should not mix benzos that you no longer have a prescription for, even in small amounts, with seroquel. Combining two sedatives can be unpredictable and dangerous, increasing risks of serotonin syndrome or severe respiratory depression. Please talk to your doctor about adjusting your dosing or trying alternative strategies, such as sleep hygiene techniques or melatonin, which are safer for beginners.",
